9" "q-158116/selection/b98c75978bde456aa326afbfe8873f3f4c2f71e93c3e48303cea7da9223fb54a" "q-158116/selection/f6a9d8d755e4acec8f8009645fcdb9a70d5f9abc39f089b80e956e6aad58f917" "q-158116/selection/8e38411da1c0a72163557785b93f667db895ac41f2d3f09c4acb37cab139e96d" "q-158116/selection/fb1d22e8839e8c28505b0e3526cce228cc708eca89166157cf13ad3864da1ce6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158116" :question/id #uuid "dd5a53b4-3b4c-5ea6-ba65-9e6d933033dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-158116" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y}$ for $x\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-154359"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-14257"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y)=x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256/selection/2d4c82822db9762b8b3f351f8ff623da3268d284ff7de947763ff3130376474d" :answer/id #uuid "6ce0949a-0ea0-5360-adbf-f161a9ff3f2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256/selection/b90df6ef46cf669ab8ac163bdcb140829c29e99aa3b592884ba5298dfc3f02bf" :answer/id #uuid "d280d431-b9b1-558d-accc-d726f6290102" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256/selection/911e22bb4ca46f36e1b61269e1af4e4b7e58cc3f55890abadb3454352926f6de" :answer/id #uuid "ac82fc84-dfaa-51f4-b138-ae94c4b491b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{6x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256/selection/ea6deee2521f66e93c19f39ec87886af25e1743a54be9bb4ece9914ece89d51c" :answer/id #uuid "6642f64e-99b2-5e95-9f2a-31c65e5a51e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=(6x+C)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256/selection/335b5c0164ca5c36859d67583ba1b333c56f60e37e8d1e9735af009c8fdc14a7" :answer/id #uuid "a387ccd1-f06b-5ffe-b783-cb8b81fbbe33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{6}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1296824-4d0d-5645-aae2-6b215316cc08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51256/selection/b90df6ef46cf669ab8ac163bdcb140829c29e99aa3b592884ba5298dfc3f02bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-51256/selection/2d4c82822db9762b8b3f351f8ff623da3268d284ff7de947763ff3130376474d" "q-51256/selection/b90df6ef46cf669ab8ac163bdcb140829c29e99aa3b592884ba5298dfc3f02bf" "q-51256/selection/911e22bb4ca46f36e1b61269e1af4e4b7e58cc3f55890abadb3454352926f6de" "q-51256/selection/ea6deee2521f66e93c19f39ec87886af25e1743a54be9bb4ece9914ece89d51c" "q-51256/selection/335b5c0164ca5c36859d67583ba1b333c56f60e37e8d1e9735af009c8fdc14a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51256" :question/id #uuid "52368e24-e78c-5f40-b95b-9857942b42f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-51256" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\int {y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{1/3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51256/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015/selection/6af031268eb97321bc84dbdee8106612a06f0dd89f7e4654e4d2e18f16d126ab" :answer/id #uuid "ca569834-7a06-5577-a89b-05cf7a434403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015/selection/6db1413f91ebc36c3194aff5d27eb472dc4f9237a31ecf06bc1b0e3bf5fa9349" :answer/id #uuid "385293a5-4745-5d8d-9510-745ea2fdd6ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015/selection/79507badd99c3742de5a45d46edaefd4efc2b8ea9c2789b27d45574c7bdcc642" :answer/id #uuid "4f628a40-0ad0-5878-a01b-3f64ab8e9acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015/selection/df80ef9133896db93ae81e7382569c4dae4cd0b96e85e7c3390c4ffda107d9fe" :answer/id #uuid "5efdd532-6f05-56a6-b2d9-aaaabdc00bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015/selection/3349baa940eee74737d3845f012ec8e839b433d6fb3cefc2ff8548927000cf7f" :answer/id #uuid "018c861f-096a-5764-8c26-2b3e6957adba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11ee4694-619b-5a20-822c-d5351e63b769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158015/selection/79507badd99c3742de5a45d46edaefd4efc2b8ea9c2789b27d45574c7bdcc642" :answer-field/choices ["q-158015/selection/6af031268eb97321bc84dbdee8106612a06f0dd89f7e4654e4d2e18f16d126ab" "q-158015/selection/6db1413f91ebc36c3194aff5d27eb472dc4f9237a31ecf06bc1b0e3bf5fa9349" "q-158015/selection/79507badd99c3742de5a45d46edaefd4efc2b8ea9c2789b27d45574c7bdcc642" "q-158015/selection/df80ef9133896db93ae81e7382569c4dae4cd0b96e85e7c3390c4ffda107d9fe" "q-158015/selection/3349baa940eee74737d3845f012ec8e839b433d6fb3cefc2ff8548927000cf7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158015" :question/id #uuid "e27324f6-57f8-5203-af7c-d98f25ea6d41" :question/math-academy-id "q-158015" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-158015/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8305"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=0$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8303"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y}=2x\\sqrt{y}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304/selection/1c3a685fcdbc520946ac62b925babbc6037fbb5034b5999ee4211f4c17b49d3a" :answer/id #uuid "152a4131-f981-5e19-bc2b-581bd3c7a741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={({x}^{2/3}+K)}^{1/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304/selection/0414aee72dd1f54c1fb131bb5a40378f3977ac94e34fff9a8e3916a2d319667b" :answer/id #uuid "a6ab1061-b24b-53f0-a11f-e4d8ef185175" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={({x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304/selection/d09fb228d0cbf1719d2300c19b2e4b2a2f00c5f8e0a4f9301c386abda6d03593" :answer/id #uuid "97acee09-353a-5f18-a0ce-d07def6bc92f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{x}^{1/2}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304/selection/1ba01d85644645bfd8b043ba3d059eaf686e8959fd9c7dd2dc7ebb43c33be227" :answer/id #uuid "09bbf700-f6cb-50e8-a453-bc5470a5818e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304/selection/cc6f1f3608a5c02bda070f9716aa5b0f35a03a1e9f4e564ff00a640642b491e6" :answer/id #uuid "98e72c92-6a3e-5cb9-93ca-61b6c716120a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3{x}^{1/3}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d59afe4-4677-55e3-b49d-ea05d784509b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8304/selection/1ba01d85644645bfd8b043ba3d059eaf686e8959fd9c7dd2dc7ebb43c33be227" :answer-field/choices ["q-8304/selection/1c3a685fcdbc520946ac62b925babbc6037fbb5034b5999ee4211f4c17b49d3a" "q-8304/selection/0414aee72dd1f54c1fb131bb5a40378f3977ac94e34fff9a8e3916a2d319667b" "q-8304/selection/d09fb228d0cbf1719d2300c19b2e4b2a2f00c5f8e0a4f9301c386abda6d03593" "q-8304/selection/1ba01d85644645bfd8b043ba3d059eaf686e8959fd9c7dd2dc7ebb43c33be227" "q-8304/selection/cc6f1f3608a5c02bda070f9716aa5b0f35a03a1e9f4e564ff00a640642b491e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8304" :question/id #uuid "b2fec0e0-010f-5a18-9431-739791e0738f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8304" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{xy}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2}=2{x}^{1/2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3/2} & =2{x}^{1/2}+C \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & =3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{3C}{2})}^{2/3} \\\\ y & ={(3{x}^{1/2}+K)}^{2/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\frac{3C}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8304/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660/selection/97bcf5fba3d49accea72ad104749bd64444ac8fd4eb823d6d887ec7508509079" :answer/id #uuid "c47617d4-fbea-57bb-9f75-7819b3be9119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{1}{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660/selection/043050eb57911e8098a44f8f91ca7da7065187057e3ad32292addd7a7f438006" :answer/id #uuid "631a1f34-a6a8-51f5-8f2f-3bedee998ee7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{K}{x}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660/selection/d749e372928dbe5ab9fe161177b4013ef8e5bc8195ba00e44db370bd835d0be6" :answer/id #uuid "6311ef46-1b7d-59e6-afa5-8ef873bbb6d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{K+\\frac{1}{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660/selection/5f993eaaae794c826f88260347b7916f5708f18b7ff84eeb007326f1545d6cef" :answer/id #uuid "228b076b-328a-5d55-b7c6-72f2d3a21e75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660/selection/3dd0f6aae6a46501d876e6ce5e89dfcd3d4241c80635c45fe5c8c20b04db09a6" :answer/id #uuid "2ca99ae2-7f33-59d9-b6c5-0a9cf0672a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{K-\\frac{2}{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8745ef-5fd1-5278-8f8c-d6c7bc460219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79660/selection/5f993eaaae794c826f88260347b7916f5708f18b7ff84eeb007326f1545d6cef" :answer-field/choices ["q-79660/selection/97bcf5fba3d49accea72ad104749bd64444ac8fd4eb823d6d887ec7508509079" "q-79660/selection/043050eb57911e8098a44f8f91ca7da7065187057e3ad32292addd7a7f438006" "q-79660/selection/d749e372928dbe5ab9fe161177b4013ef8e5bc8195ba00e44db370bd835d0be6" "q-79660/selection/5f993eaaae794c826f88260347b7916f5708f18b7ff84eeb007326f1545d6cef" "q-79660/selection/3dd0f6aae6a46501d876e6ce5e89dfcd3d4241c80635c45fe5c8c20b04db09a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79660" :question/id #uuid "6f16fb1d-1d77-5697-b17d-ce1113407a71" :question/math-academy-id "q-79660" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $(xy)^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(xy)^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}=C-\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3} & =C-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3C-\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{3C-\\frac{3}{x}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{K-\\frac{3}{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=3C.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79660/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
